  "the_wire": {
    "conversion_happens_in": "tools/mtmd/mtmd-helper.cpp::decode_audio_from_buf -- miniaudio, ma_decoder_config_init(ma_format_f32, 1, mtmd_get_audio_sample_rate) = 16000, which for a 24 kHz file is a RESAMPLE, not a format cast",
    "server_forwards": "tools/server/server-common.cpp handle_media base64-decodes the string straight into a raw_buffer and hands file.data()/file.size() to mtmd_helper_bitmap_init_from_buf. Nothing between the wire and miniaudio inspects or converts the bytes.",
    "study_sends": "core/model/transport.py::_load_audio_part -- base64.b64encode(media.read_bytes()) into an input_audio part with format taken from the file suffix. The sealed bytes go out verbatim: no resample, no trim, no normalization, no re-encode."
